  "id": "saint-lucia-water-court-estate",
  "thesis": "A single-storey waterfront estate conceived as a deeply shaded limestone-and-ivory belvedere: a tall central social hall mediates between a deliberately compressed landward arrival court and a broad south-facing pool terrace, while two long, quiet bedroom cloisters extend laterally as sheltered private arms. The composition makes the waterfront elevation a layered sequence of solid service piers, deep veranda shadow and living-room glazing rather than an indiscriminate glass wall.",
